{"files": [{"id": 47099668, "name": "ppat.1011970.g005.tif", "size": 1052844, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/47099668", "supplied_md5": "21c0ad6a965e1ca4b9a4dbbbf997f5bb", "computed_md5": "21c0ad6a965e1ca4b9a4dbbbf997f5bb", "mimetype": "image/tiff"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 4308, "full_name": "Yan Chen", "first_name": "Yan", "last_name": "Chen", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Yan_Chen", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841048, "full_name": "Rodney P. Kincaid", "first_name": "Rodney P.", "last_name": "Kincaid", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841051, "full_name": "Kelley Bastin", "first_name": "Kelley", "last_name": "Bastin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841054, "full_name": "Devin N. Fachko", "first_name": "Devin N.", "last_name": "Fachko", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841057, "full_name": "Rebecca L. Skalsky", "first_name": "Rebecca L.", "last_name": "Skalsky", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Chemical_inhibition_of_the_Raf_Mek_Erk_pathway_limits_lytic_reactivation_in_miR-142_mutant_cells_/26051935", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>A. Schematic illustration of the Ras/Raf/Mek/Erk kinase cascade and the protein targets of dabrafenib and cobimetinib. B. Immunoblot validation of cobimetinib activity in miR-142 mutant MutuI cells (10024.C19) in blocking phosphorylation of Erk by Mek. Gapdh levels are shown as loading controls. C. Immunoblot validation of dabrafenib activity in miR-142 mutant MutuI cells (10024.C19) in blocking phosphorylation of Mek by Raf. Gapdh levels are shown as loading controls. D. and E. Band intensities in panels B. and C. were quantified using ImageJ and normalized to loading controls. Ratios of phospho-proteins to total proteins were reported relative to 0 min. Shown are the averages of three independent experiments. Student\u2019s t-test, *p<0.05. F. and G. EBV lytic proteins are reduced in miR-142 mutant MutuI cells upon inhibition of the Raf/Mek/Erk pathway. 10024.C19 cells were treated with either cobimetinib or dabrafenib followed by anti-IgM for 24 hrs. Zta and Ea-D were assayed by immunoblot. Beta-actin levels are shown as loading controls. Shown are representative images of three independent experiments. H. and I. Band intensities in panels F. and G. were quantified using ImageJ and normalized to loading controls. Shown are the averages of three independent experiments. Student\u2019s t-test, *p<0.05.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 1052844, "created_date": "2024-06-17T17:37:29Z", "modified_date": "2024-06-28T17:35:37Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["b cell receptor", "surface ig cross", "xlink \"> reactivation", "142 targets related", "142 enhanced levels", "restricts ebv entry", "support viral infection", "infected bl cells", "cells using anti", "ebv lytic phase", "erk signaling initiated", "ebv reactivation", "mapk signaling", "lytic stage", "ig antibodies", "induce reactivation", "ebv latency", "taken together", "significant role", "results show", "latency plays", "key regulator", "immediate early", "grna library", "genetic ablation", "gain insight", "fully understood", "effects could", "dabrafenib ).", "clip experiments", "burkitt lymphoma", "based screen", "barr virus"], "keywords": ["b cell receptor", "surface ig cross", "xlink \"> reactivation", "142 targets related", "142 enhanced levels", "restricts ebv entry", "support viral infection", "infected bl cells", "cells using anti", "ebv lytic phase", "erk signaling initiated", "ebv reactivation", "mapk signaling",